
# Basics - Reading Data

  Query	and What it does :-

  Fetch all columns, all rows ->
  SELECT * FROM orders;

  Fetch specific columns only ->
  SELECT id, amount FROM orders;

  Unique values in a column ->
  SELECT DISTINCT status FROM orders;

  Filter rows ->
  SELECT * FROM orders WHERE status = 'PAID';

  Combine conditions (AND/OR/NOT) ->
  SELECT * FROM orders WHERE amount > 1000 AND status = 'PAID';

  Match any value in a list ->
  SELECT * FROM orders WHERE status IN ('PAID','REFUNDED');

  Range filter (inclusive) ->
  SELECT * FROM orders WHERE amount BETWEEN 100 AND 500;

  Pattern match (%=any chars, _=one char) ->
  SELECT * FROM orders WHERE customer_name LIKE 'A%';

  Check for NULL (never use = NULL) ->
  SELECT * FROM orders WHERE deleted_at IS NULL;

  Sort (ASC default, DESC for newest first)->
  SELECT * FROM orders ORDER BY created_at DESC;

  Cap the number of rows returned ->
  SELECT * FROM orders LIMIT 10;

  Pagination — skip 20, take next 10 ->
  SELECT * FROM orders LIMIT 10 OFFSET 20;

  Top-1 by some metric ->
  SELECT * FROM orders ORDER BY amount DESC LIMIT 1;
